00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:21,000
Zombi 2 is a 1979 English-language Italian zombie film directed by Lucio Fulci.

12
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
It was adapted from an original screenplay by Dardano
Sacchetti to serve as a sequel to George A.

13
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:51,000
Romero's Dawn of the Dead (1978), which was
released in Italy under the title Zombi.

14
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
The film was released as Zombie in the United States and
Zombie Flesh-Eaters in the United Kingdom.

15
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:21,000
It stars Tisa Farrow, Ian McCulloch, and Richard Johnson, and features
a score by frequent Fulci collaborator Fabio Frizzi.

16
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The film is set on a Caribbean island cursed by voodoo whose dead
residents rise as zombies to attack the living.

17
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:51,000
A scientist's daughter journeys to the island after her
father's boat turns up abandoned in New York City.

18
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
Intended by its writer as a return to "classic zombie tales", Zombi 2 was filmed in
Italy, with further location shooting in New York and Santo Domingo.

19
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
Produced on a small budget of 410 million Italian lira, the film earned
several times its production costs back in international gross.

20
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
It attracted controversy upon its release in the United
Kingdom, where it became listed as a "video nasty".

21
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
However, in the subsequent years the film received a greater
appreciation from critics, and has gained a cult following.

22
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
The film explores themes of monster, mad
scientist, zombie animals, zombie, shark.

23
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:21,000
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
